+# Locked 26.2 failed-upgrade settlement patch
+
+Original C2ME revision: `e5f9ed26349b2f9504f73cac48aa09a490d137a3`
+(`0.4.2+alpha.0-43-ge5f9ed26`). Original FlowSched:
+`fae2126839607b68d4059e3933a492886fe8b8f5`.
+FlowSched fix: `f5634c0a64b952da9e2961fa724da136b51585cf`.
+
+The native MARK_BROKEN upgrade branch previously released action/busy state but
+left DISK and dependent status requesters pending. Removing demand eventually
+substituted generic Not loaded. The fix validates the exact action, target and
+status slot, retains the original failure on this holder, publishes prefailed
+replacement slots under the holder monitor, and signals captured requesters and
+dependency tickets after releasing that monitor. Later demand on this broken
+holder fails immediately. Actual holder removal permits a fresh generation.
+Successful lower statuses, native demand accounting and normal unload remain.
+
+Three FlowSched classes change: ItemHolder, ItemTicket and
+StatusAdvancingScheduler. Eleven separate contract tests exercise failure,
+local/later/cross-holder dependents, replacement, unload, race orderings, multiple
+requesters and callback reentry/lock safety. The original Phoenium characterization
+is retained unchanged against the original binary. The eleven tests also pass
+with the exact settlement2 nested base ahead of source classes on the test
+classpath. Phoenium's packaged-native availability test supplies only a future
+to the original or patched native getter and checks pending, failed, cancelled
+and successful results.
+
+Settled failures exposed one native nullable-peek assumption: the rewrites
+module's NewChunkHolderVanillaInterface.getWorldChunk (runtime getTickingChunk)
+called getNow on an exceptional explicit requester future. Its nullable lookup
+now returns only a successfully available chunk; the explicit future retains
+the original error. This prevents failure reporting from crashing ordinary
+ticking and shutdown. It does not convert failed requests into successes.
+
+## Artifact
+
+* Original SHA-256: `B013229383F51789C57684CBCFC12981C8D791206F3B594866DFEB74AED3770B`
+* Output: `build/patched/c2me-0.4.2-alpha.0.43+26.2-phoenium-settlement2.jar`
+* Version: `0.4.2-alpha.0.43-phoenium-settlement2+26.2`
+* Size: 3,834,439 bytes
+* SHA-256: `8AE4F2BB5FB15A28E555816DE89F0E400EA6A55A11213673E60068BC43C13D53`
+* Nested base SHA-256: `DBEA700B7675C4A6CA7E8F48D0D6554CDDA5B9C36F01B6588FDEBE5302E5732D`
+* Nested rewrites SHA-256: `065C2A842FFB5DE66CC35E9F627AD6D79A84B0918BC7CEF8DE1C1D297A004625`
+
+The adjacent machine manifest records original nested identities, touched entry
+payloads, compiled class hashes and Java identity. Every other ZIP entry payload
+is byte-identical to the locked original. Original and settlement1 artifacts are
+preserved. No newer provider release is substituted.
+
+Build with Java Temurin 25.0.4.1+1-LTS from this source root:
+
+```powershell
+.\gradlew.bat :c2me-rewrites-chunk-system:remapJar --no-daemon
+python build-settlement.py ../Phoenium/build/stage6-audit-20260909/research/artifacts/c2me/c2me-fabric-mc26.2-0.4.2-alpha.0.43.jar build/patched/c2me-0.4.2-alpha.0.43+26.2-phoenium-settlement2.jar --rewrites c2me-rewrites-chunk-system/build/libs/c2me-fabric-rewrites-chunk-system-mc26.2-0.4.2-alpha.0.43-dirty.jar
+```
+
+The output builder refuses to overwrite an artifact. The remapped input filename
+is the exact input used before this local root commit; future rebuilds must pass
+the filename Gradle actually emits and verify its native class diff. ZIP
+container timestamps can differ on regeneration; acceptance pins the artifact
+above, not an assumed reproducible hash from an arbitrary later checkout.
+
+This is a reasonable small upstream proposal: holder-local failed requester and
+dependency settlement belongs in FlowSched; the nullable native lookup belongs
+in C2ME. Project metadata/version packaging is local integration. No push or
+upstream submission has been made. The provider submodule commit is local and
+must travel with this checkout or an exported patch.
+
+Phoenium's independent lifetime/co-install acceptance is recorded in its
+`docs/STAGE7_C2ME_LIFETIME_DECISION.md`; this native manifest alone does not clear
+that gate or authorize removal of Phoenium's production exclusions.
